<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43920" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐήνωρ</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐάνωρ</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ορος</span>, ὁ,
				ἡ</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> (only in <i><span class="en">
			Od.
		</span></i>), prob. '<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the joy of
			men</i>', 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρον δ᾽ εὐήνορα οἶνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.622
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρον δ᾽ εὐήνορα χαλκόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					13.19
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> later, of
			communities, etc., <i>well-manned, abounding in brave men</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				1.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.80
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>N.</u>
					10.36
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππος</span>, of the Trojan
			horse, <i><span class="en">
				Tryph.
				468
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
